{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>You have shown</b> — this too is in the force of the active participle: <b>you have shown your people hard things</b> — a harsh vision, and it is as the hitpa'el of <b>השקיתנו יין תרעלה</b> (You have made us drink wine of staggering), and the form of <b>השקיתנו יין תרעלה</b> is like the Book of the Makneh, and likewise here <b>זה יין תרעלה</b> is construct state."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's Hebrew is cryptic and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally without smoothing. The reference to 'the Book of the Makneh' is obscure; 'ספר המקנה' read as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:21.960832397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}